-- title:
--   Igusa components of the descended two-chart model, q=3
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=3$, let $M'\neq 0$ with $q\nmid M'$, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $q$ is a nonunit, write $k$ for its residue field, and let $W$ be a finite set of places of the level-$M'$ modular function field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,M'$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places (rational, affine geometric, with supersingular $j$-value). Assume the base-changed full level-$M'$ field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ is contained in the geometric level field $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, and let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ along $A$ with values in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,k\,M'$ such that every Laurent series with coefficients in $A$ lying in that field is $R_0$-integral with residue its coefficientwise reduction. Let $\pi\in A$ satisfy $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$, let $\zeta$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity, and let $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$, indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$, and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$, indexed by $W$, be families of valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ subject to: membership of $f$ in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ is the existence of Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ of nonzero reduction and $f\cdot y=x$; each index $\ell$ is $\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma\cdot\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q$ for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the preimage of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ under $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$; injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$; and pullback along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ permuting the family for all $\zeta'$ and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; for $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$: its constants are exactly $A$; each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is fixed by all these automorphisms; for every $s$ there is $t\in O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ with $t-a$ a unit for all $a\in A$; and a compatibility (summarised here) asserting that an $R_0$-integral $f$ whose order is non-negative at every place where that of the $q$-expansion of $j$ is, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, has its image in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, congruent modulo the maximal ideal to any $a\in A$ whose residue is the value of that $R_0$-residue at $s$. Let further $K_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ be a subfield with $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ algebraic over it and $\pi\in K_0$, let $A_0$ be a henselian discrete valuation domain with maximal ideal $(\varpi_0)$ and an injective local homomorphism $\iota:A_0\to A$ with image $A\cap K_0$, surjective on residues, and $\iota\varpi_0=\pi$; let $F_0$ be the subfield of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of series all of whose coefficients lie in $K_0$, containing the image $\hat\jmath$ of the $q$-expansion of $j$, with $\hat\jmath\neq 0$, and with an $A_0$-algebra structure on $F_0$ induced by $\iota$; finally let $S=\{\hat\jmath\}$ or $S=\{\hat\jmath^{-1}\}$. Write $C=\mathrm{chartAlg}\,A_0\,F_0\,S$ for the $A_0$-subalgebra of $F_0$ of elements integral over $A_0[S]$. Then there is a family $\mathfrak q$ of ideals of $C$ indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ such that: for each $\ell$ and each $x\in F_0$, the image of $x$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ if and only if $x=b/c$ with $b,c\in C$ and $c\notin\mathfrak q(\ell)$; each $\mathfrak q(\ell)$ is a minimal prime over the ideal of $C$ generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $A_0$; $\mathfrak q$ is injective; and every minimal prime over that ideal is $\mathfrak q(\ell)$ for some $\ell$.
--
--   This is the component structure of the special fibre of the descended two-chart integral model: for either chart algebra, the minimal primes over $\varpi_0$ are in bijection with $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$ and their localisations are the traces on $F_0$ of the Igusa valuation rings, in the case $q=3$. It is used in the subsequent identifications of maximal ideals of the Igusa and Drinfeld rings inside the descended chart algebras, which enter the semistable covering of modular curves at $q$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_exists_primes_chartAlg_localization_eq_igusaRing_minimal_injective_descent_of_eq_three.lean

